.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt DDI_FAULT_EVENT_DATA 9S
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ddi_fault_event_data
.Nd payload of a device fault event
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBstruct ddi_fault_event_data\fP is the event-specific payload for
\fBDDI_DEVI_FAULT_EVENT\fP, whose event name is \fBDDI:DEVI_FAULT\fP.
\fBddi_dev_report_fault()\fP assembles the payload and posts it through the NDI
event framework.
An event callback receives a pointer to it as the bus implementation data.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va f_dip
Device node reporting the fault.
.It Va f_impact
Impact on device service, expressed as \fBddi_fault_impact_t\fP, such as
\fBDDI_SERVICE_LOST\fP, \fBDDI_SERVICE_DEGRADED\fP, \fBDDI_SERVICE_UNAFFECTED\fP, or
\fBDDI_SERVICE_RESTORED\fP.
.It Va f_location
Fault location classification, expressed as \fBddi_fault_location_t\fP.
.It Va f_message
Borrowed pointer to the diagnostic message supplied by the reporter.
.It Va f_oldstate
Device state obtained before the fault event is posted.
.El
.Pp
The reporting function uses a temporary payload and delivers the event
synchronously.
Callbacks must not retain the payload pointer after returning.
The message and device node are also borrowed; copying their pointers does
not extend the lifetime of the referenced objects.
.Sh STRUCTURE MEMBERS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dev_info_t             *f_dip;
ddi_fault_impact_t     f_impact;
ddi_fault_location_t   f_location;
const char             *f_message;
ddi_devstate_t         f_oldstate;
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ddi_dev_report_fault 9F ,
.Xr ddi_get_devstate 9F ,
.Xr ndi_post_event 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
